  "mathematical_review": "ENTIRE frozen 248-line source, every actual Euler, dehomogenization, coefficient and finite-degree induction helper, and all THREE complete written BP proofs reviewed. The genuine polynomial direction has pivot component1 and prescribed other components b_i. At each exponent on the ENTIRE original source diagram, every directional derivative coefficient shifts to another source-diagram exponent by actual upward closure, so source normality is preserved without source tangent stability. Direct polynomial induction proves actual affine dehomogenization commutes with nonpivot partial differentiation and is independent of the pivot. Applying dehomogenization to the genuine homogeneous Euler identity gives dehom(delta_v P) plus the actual target Euler operator equals d times dehom(P). A complete coefficient computation of the actual Euler operator gives its true TOTAL exponent degree, hence the literal scalar formula (d minus degree(beta)) times the dehomogeneous coefficient. Actual derivative homogeneity and finite constant summation retain degree d-1, with the genuine zero derivative case at d=0. For an actual source-normal homogeneous P of degree d and a disclosed k at most d, genuine affine substitution bounds total degree of its whole dehomogenization by d. If k=d and every lower coefficient vanishes, that entire dehomogenization is genuinely homogeneous of degree d. The previously proved real homogeneous dehomogenization/shear identity identifies it with the ACTUAL linear source shear of P. Membership of its whole band in the ENTIRE sheared source initial ideal then contracts by the genuine inverse shear to membership of P in the source initial ideal. Its diagram equals the original source diagram, where P has zero coefficients, so actual normal uniqueness forces P=0. For d>k, the genuine directional derivative is homogeneous of degree d-1 and source normal; its entire dehomogenization has the same low-band vanishing and k-band EXACTLY the nonzero complex scalar d-k times the original k-band. Whole sheared ideal membership is retained by true scalar ideal closure. Strong induction in d with k retained kills that derivative band; characteristic zero scalar cancellation kills the original band. This is a genuine finite degree induction, not a source/current diagram inclusion assumption. Finally each SAME canonical reduced-source homogeneous band of degree strictly above its original vertex has all source-diagram coefficients zero internally: canonical sparsity leaves only the vertex, whose degree cannot equal that higher degree. The actual finite homogeneous polynomial construction gives its homogeneity, so the preceding theorem applies with the explicitly retained finite low-dehom vanishing and sheared source-initial membership hypotheses. No first offending CURRENT quotient-band extraction, current order retention or whole HS criterion is inferred from these qualified finite algebra statements.",
